Cumulus
-------

Displays a 14-day weather forecast with minimum and maximum temperatures and
the probability of rain.

Cumulus is a KDE Plasma 6 applet (plasmoid) written in C++ and QML.
Plugin ID: io.github.leghissa.cumulus


-- Requirements --

* Qt >= 6.7 (Core, Gui, Quick)
* KDE Frameworks 6 (I18n, Config) and Extra CMake Modules
* Plasma 6 (libplasma, plasmoidviewer for testing)
* CMake >= 3.16


-- Build instructions --

cmake -S . -B ../Cumulus_build -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Debug
cmake --build ../Cumulus_build

To use the applet in the running Plasma session, install it and restart
plasmashell:

sudo cmake --install ../Cumulus_build
kquitapp6 plasmashell && plasmashell

(The install prefix defaults to /usr; set -DCMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX when
configuring to install elsewhere.)


-- Testing & Developing --

Cumulus is a compiled applet: the QML files and images are embedded in the
plugin library (bin/plasma/applets/io.github.leghissa.cumulus.so in the build
directory). It therefore has to be loaded by its plugin ID, not by a path.
"plasmoidviewer -a src/" does NOT work and fails with
"File name empty! ... Invalid empty URL".

From the command line, run the freshly built applet without installing it:

tools/run-plasmoidviewer.sh

The script points QT_PLUGIN_PATH at ../Cumulus_build/bin and starts
"plasmoidviewer -a io.github.leghissa.cumulus --formfactor planar".
Set CUMULUS_BUILD_DIR to use a different build directory. Any arguments are
passed on to plasmoidviewer instead of the default, e.g.:

tools/run-plasmoidviewer.sh --formfactor vertical --location leftedge

Launch configuration in KDevelop:

1. Run > Configure Launches...
2. Select the project "Cumulus" and add a new "Compiled Binary" launch
   (do not use the "Plasmoid Launcher" type, see below).
3. Executable: choose "Executable" and enter the absolute path to
   tools/run-plasmoidviewer.sh in this repository.
4. Arguments: leave empty.
5. Working Directory: the repository root.
6. Dependencies: add the target io.github.leghissa.cumulus and set the
   action to "Build", so every launch builds the applet first.
7. Save, then start it with Run > Execute Launch (Shift+F9).

Why not set this up differently:
* The "Plasmoid Launcher" type passes a path or ID to plasmoidviewer but
  cannot set QT_PLUGIN_PATH, so it cannot find an applet that is only in the
  build directory.
* KDevelop rejects shell metacharacters (including "=") in launch arguments
  ("A shell meta character was included in the arguments ..."), so
  "QT_PLUGIN_PATH=... plasmoidviewer ..." cannot be entered directly. That is
  why the wrapper script exists.


-- Translations --

Messages.sh extracts translatable strings (translation domain
plasma_applet_io.github.leghissa.cumulus) for KDE's i18n tooling.


